  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\nMarch 9-13, 2020 WWWceraweek com\n\n## Media Registration is Now Open for CERAWeek by IHS Markit 2020\n\nApplications for media registration can be submitted at the following link: https:Ilbit.lyl2LoeSGU\n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation:.\n\nComplete details related to media registration are included below in this email.\n\n## About CERAWeek 2020\n\nCERAWeek 2020 will kick off Monday, March 9 at the Hilton Americas-Houston:\n\nCERAWeek by IHS Markit is the premier annual international gathering of energy industry leaders; experts; government officials and policymakers; leaders from the technology; financial and industrial communities and energy technology innovators. Chaired by Daniel Yergin; CERAWeek 2020 will be the events 39th installment:.\n\nVisit www ceraweek com for the most up-to-date event information and follow us via @CERAWeek. Listed session times; topics and speakers are subject to change.\n\n## Media Registration Details:\n\nAll members of the media interested in attending CERAWeek 2020 are required to apply for accreditation:.\n\nJournalists should submit their request for media registration at the following link:\n\nAs always, the CERAWeek Media Relations Team is happy to provide a designated media work room as of our conference-wide efforts to make journalists' experiences convenient and productive at the conference. part\n\n## CERAWeek 2020 Media Work Room Amenities:\n\n- Fully-staffed Media Work Room adjacent to the CERAWeek Briefing Room",
